---
/**
 * Tech design §18's sizing table, and what the "$20 server" on the landing page means. The
 * table scrolls on phones, so its wrapper is focusable for keyboard users.
 */
import { SIZING, STATUS } from '../../data/self-hosting.ts';
import Badge from '../site/Badge.astro';
import Section from '../site/Section.astro';
---

<Section title="Sizing and cost" id="sizing">
  <div tabindex="0" class="overflow-x-auto rounded-card border border-line">
    <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-14">
      <thead class="bg-side text-12 font-semibold tracking-caps text-tx-3 uppercase dark:bg-card">
        <tr>
          <th class="px-3.5 py-2.5 font-semibold">Team</th>
          <th class="px-3.5 py-2.5 font-semibold">Server</th>
          <th class="px-3.5 py-2.5 font-semibold">What to expect</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {SIZING.map((row) => (
          <tr class="border-t border-line-2 align-top">
            <td class="px-3.5 py-2.5 font-medium whitespace-nowrap text-tx">{row.team}</td>
            <td class="px-3.5 py-2.5 whitespace-nowrap">
              <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
                {row.vm}
                {row.status && (
                  <Badge tone={STATUS[row.status].tone}>{STATUS[row.status].label}</Badge>
                )}
              </span>
            </td>
            <td class="px-3.5 py-2.5">{row.note}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    The “$20 server” is the second row: a 2 vCPU, 4 GB VM lists at roughly $5 to $25 a month with
    common cloud and VPS providers, and Bemmoly adds no licence or per-seat fee on top.
  </p>
</Section>
